import AspisFormal.K1.V7Tag73AtomicForkUniformScheduler
import AspisFormal.K1.V7Tag73ConcreteKnowledgeInsertion

/-!
# Strict finite lazy-ROM probability and K1.6-ready arithmetic

This module records the strongest unconditional probability statement
currently provided by the operational Tag-73 lazy-oracle stack.  One fixed
finite master experiment samples

* an arbitrary finite hidden adversary tape; and
* exactly `F` independent uniform 256-bit coordinates,

where

`F = full256FreshExposures + 2 * restorationCount`.

The corresponding strict global call cap is

`G = q1Calls + verifierOracleCalls +
       restorationCount * oracleCallsPerRestoration`.

The adaptive scheduler's collision/literal-prefix target event is bounded by
the exact causal coefficient

`choose(F, 2) + F * G`.

No BCS coefficient, compiler cover, restoration function, witness-extraction
conclusion, or event-wise independence premise occurs here.  The arithmetic
section consumes only the explicitly typed K1.2--K1.5 knowledge inequality.
Its left side remains the sum of the concrete interactive-event probability
and the scheduler target-event probability.  Replacing that sum by deployed
Fiat--Shamir acceptance still requires the protocol-specific operational
set-inclusion theorem; it is intentionally neither assumed nor renamed in
this file.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace AspisK1.V7Tag73StrictLazyRomAokArithmetic

open MeasureTheory
open AspisK1.V7FsAokExperiment
open AspisK1.V7FsStateRestorationCoupling
open AspisK1.V7Tag73TranscriptSchedule
open AspisK1.V7Tag73AdaptiveLazyOracle
